{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c2b31fb9-e131-6465-dd82-068dcdda62f2",
    "name": "TmsIntern API",
    "description": "# TmsIntern API\n\nHand-documented Postman collection for the TmsIntern platform, built\nfrom version-controlled fragments under `postman/build/fragments`. Rebuild it\nwith `postman/build.sh` (bash) or `postman/build.ps1` (PowerShell).\n\n## Authentication\n\nAuth uses **Laravel Sanctum** with two token abilities:\n\n- `access` — used by virtually every protected endpoint.\n- `refresh` — used **only** by `POST /user/refresh`.\n\nThe collection default auth is **Bearer `{{access_token}}`**, so protected\nrequests inherit it automatically. Public requests override this with *No Auth*.\n\n`Verify OTP` and `Refresh access token` include test scripts that\ncapture the returned tokens into the `{{access_token}}` / `{{refresh_token}}`\ncollection variables, so you can log in once and then call protected endpoints.\n\n## Variables\n\n| Variable | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `base_url` | API root, e.g. `http://localhost:8000/api`. |\n| `access_token` | Auto-filled after verify-otp / refresh. |\n| `refresh_token` | Auto-filled after verify-otp / refresh. |\n| `lang` | Sent as the `lang` header (`ar` or `en`). Defaults to `ar`. |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
